.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-SCIM" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-scim - Directory sync (SCIM) for a team (owners and admins)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team scim [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Directory sync for a team through WorkOS: connect your company directory (Okta, Entra ID, Google Workspace and others) and Paperboat adds, updates and removes members to match it within seconds. Map directory groups to team roles. Removing someone in the directory removes them from the team at once and ends their open sessions.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for scim


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP, \fBpb-team-scim-map(1)\fP, \fBpb-team-scim-setup(1)\fP, \fBpb-team-scim-status(1)\fP
